  "worked_solution": "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve for $z$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+y & =6\\,\u27f9\\,z=6-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+(6-y)^{2} & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+(36-12y+{y}^{2}) & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-12y+36 & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by completing the square for the variable $y$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-12y+36 & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-12{y}^{2}+18 & =6 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2({y}^{2}-6{y}^{2}+9) & =6 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2(y-3)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{3} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{3}=1.$",
